  "t-parts": {
   "x": 0,
   "y": -320,
   "text": "Building blocks — identity and shared parts",
   "kind": "title1",
   "maxW": 1440,
   "page": "parts"
  },
  "s-parts": {
   "x": -700,
   "y": 1300,
   "w": 560,
   "maxH": 700,
   "page": "parts",
   "fill": "blue",
   "size": "m",
   "text": "Layout rules from review\n\n• No scrollbars: every desktop screen fits a 1440 × 900 window. Tables wrap text instead of scrolling sideways; long lists paginate; secondary detail goes into tabs or a side column. Only the phone scrolls.\n• The side menu never collapses: every section is always open. Rows are 30 px so the full admin menu (22 items) fits without scrolling. Help is the ? in the top bar.\n• The top bar and side menu stay fixed; only the page content moves if anything ever scrolls.\n• Instance IDs are shown to Administrators only, everywhere. The server leaves them out of every response for anyone else (environment pages, VM details, registry, activity and audit text, error messages), so hiding them doesn't rely on the screen. IP addresses are visible to everyone who can see the environment."
  },
