   "w": 560,
   "maxH": 900,
   "page": "details",
   "fill": "blue",
   "size": "m",
   "text": "Everything that opens from the environment page, VM registry and cost pages.\n\n• VM details: one panel with tabs, not a long scroll. Overview, use (CPU, memory, network, disk over 1 h / 6 h / 24 h / 7 d), storage, idle detection, history. Rightsizing advice sits on the VM. The instance ID row appears for Administrators only (switch 'admin' in the panel's settings).\n• Idle auto-stop: what the dry run would have stopped and saved, snooze for anyone who uses the environment, rule settings for environment admins.\n• Starting shows live progress by start order with each VM's state, and how long it usually takes.\n• Environment settings gathers what are separate panels today (details, groups and start order, leases, idle stop, Teams channels, webhooks, Spot) into one place for environment admins.\n• Adding VMs from AWS shows name, size, zone, state and IP — no instance IDs for environment admins."
  },
